        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$lld and %2$lld fill these two squares between them, so neither can go anywhere else in column %3$lld."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "coach.nakedPair.sentence.row" : {
      "comment" : "Coach explanation, naked pair clearing a ROW: two digits fill two squares between them, so neither can appear elsewhere in that row. %1$lld and %2$lld are the two digits, %3$lld the row number.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$lld and %2$lld fill these two squares between them, so neither can go anywhere else in row %3$lld."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "coach.nakedSingle.sentence" : {
      "comment" : "Coach explanation, naked single: this square has only one candidate left. %1$lld is the row (1-9), %2$lld the column (1-9), %3$lld the digit. Sentence-initial in English; put the square wherever your language puts it.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Row %1$lld, column %2$lld has one candidate left: %3$lld."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "coach.slip.sentence" : {
      "comment" : "Coach card body when two squares contradict each other. Says that nothing can follow, without saying which square is wrong.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Two of these squares disagree, so nothing can follow from here."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "coach.slip.title" : {
      "comment" : "Coach card heading when two squares contradict each other, so no hint is possible. Gentle and blameless: the player made a slip, they did not fail.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A slip somewhere"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "coach.solved.title" : {
      "comment" : "Coach card heading when the board is finished. One word.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Done"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "coach.xWing.sentence.colBase" : {
      "comment" : "Coach explanation, X-wing based on two COLUMNS: in two columns the digit can only sit in the same two rows, so it is cleared from the rest of those rows. %1$lld is the digit and appears twice.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "In these two columns, %1$lld can only sit in two rows, so no other square in those rows can be a %1$lld."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "coach.xWing.sentence.rowBase" : {
      "comment" : "Coach explanation, X-wing based on two ROWS: in two rows the digit can only sit in the same two columns, so it is cleared from the rest of those columns. %1$lld is the digit and appears TWICE — move both if you reorder. The words \"rows\" and \"columns\" are part of the sentence; write them the way your language names them.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "In these two rows, %1$lld can only sit in two columns, so no other square in those columns can be a %1$lld."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "difficulty.composeCaption" : {
      "comment" : "Shown in place of a difficulty card's blurb while that band's board is being generated, which can take seconds. %1$@ is the band's name. An honest apology for a wait, not a progress report.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ takes a moment to compose"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "difficulty.gentle.blurb" : {
      "comment" : "One-line blurb under the Gentle difficulty card: the two sudoku techniques its boards need. Both are terms of art — use this language's puzzle vocabulary. Very short; it sits under a 64pt tile.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Singles & scans"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "difficulty.gentle.explainer" : {
      "comment" : "The longer explanation of the Gentle band, in the difficulty guide. \"A single\" is the sudoku term for a square with only one possibility. Two short sentences — the guide has no room to scroll.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Every step is a single: one place a digit can go. A calm first board."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "difficulty.gentle.title" : {
      "comment" : "Difficulty band, easiest of four. Shown on buttons and menus and on the share card. An adjective in the app's calm register — not \"Easy\", which sounds like a judgement of the player. One or two words.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gentle"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "difficulty.nocturne.blurb" : {
      "comment" : "One-line blurb under the Nocturne difficulty card. \"Clues\" are the digits the puzzle supplies; Nocturne gives fewer of them than any other band. Very short.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fewer clues, deeper logic"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "difficulty.nocturne.explainer" : {
      "comment" : "The longer explanation of the Nocturne band. \"Sharp\" here is the name of the band below it — translate it the same way as `difficulty.sharp.title`. \"Givens\" are the digits the puzzle supplies. One sentence, kept to the length of its three siblings so the guide still fits one screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sharp's logic at the clue floor: fewer givens, more of the hard steps."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "difficulty.nocturne.title" : {
      "comment" : "Difficulty band, hardest of four. A night piece — the late, quiet, difficult one. Borrowing the musical term untranslated is fine where that word exists. One or two words.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nocturne"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "difficulty.sharp.blurb" : {
      "comment" : "One-line blurb under the Sharp difficulty card. \"X-wing\" is a sudoku term of art, almost always left untranslated. Very short.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "X-wings & deep logic"
